-- Restore the 21 pre-bcrypt security-question rows, exactly as they were
-- before 20260918120000_security_answer_sha256_fallback.sql.
--
-- These 21 members had their answers stored as UNSALTED SHA-256 hex by an
-- implementation retired around 2026-04-20. The current RPC compares with
-- bcrypt crypt(), which can never match a hex digest, so every one of them
-- failed password reset no matter what they typed.
--
-- The fallback migration verifies against SHA-256 and then REWRITES that
-- row's hash to bcrypt on the first successful answer. That rewrite is
-- destructive to the old value, which is why this snapshot exists: it is
-- the only copy of these digests once a member recovers.
--
-- Restoring puts a member BACK into the broken state, so only run this to
-- undo a bad migration, never as routine cleanup.

begin;

